WEBVTT

00:02.828 --> 00:04.167
But you must not run away.

00:04.986 --> 00:05.986
After all,

00:06.365 --> 00:08.012
you've already met the light along that road.

00:09.812 --> 00:10.812
- That is...
- Damn!

00:11.112 --> 00:13.060
Kyo is gonna be popular!

00:13.847 --> 00:14.514
What?!

00:14.901 --> 00:15.901
Stop it!

00:16.961 --> 00:17.693
So it'll...

00:17.693 --> 00:20.814
Whatchu gonna do if this speech
gets you a fan base?

00:21.221 --> 00:23.554
Nothing of that sort is going to happen!

00:24.157 --> 00:25.452
You don't know that.

00:26.168 --> 00:27.902
If it does, will you be able to say it?

00:28.612 --> 00:30.531
"I already have someone I like."

00:31.114 --> 00:32.073
...or something.

00:33.533 --> 00:34.993
What do you think you're saying?!

00:35.193 --> 00:37.537
No way she saw that, right...

00:38.214 --> 00:39.022
I...

00:39.356 --> 00:40.849
...already have someone I like.

00:41.462 --> 00:42.489
Let's practice!

00:42.793 --> 00:44.265
I like you, Ichikawa.

00:44.858 --> 00:46.258
Come on now!

00:48.157 --> 00:49.992
(Class 2-3)

00:54.402 --> 00:55.402
Yamada...

00:56.477 --> 00:57.657
...likes me?

01:02.143 --> 01:03.156
Even if she does,

01:03.621 --> 01:05.394
the situation hasn't really changed.

01:06.110 --> 01:08.825
In fact, doesn't that mean
I have to be more careful?

01:09.749 --> 01:11.555
Compared to her affection level
of 0 before this,

01:11.682 --> 01:14.342
the fall from a higher level
is gonna be way harsher.

01:14.783 --> 01:15.993
Careful now...

01:15.993 --> 01:16.989
No, I can't!

01:16.989 --> 01:19.637
Get a grip! I can't be
making any creepy moves.

01:21.597 --> 01:23.196
- Umm...
- Which reminds me...

01:23.953 --> 01:28.699
I'm going to karaoke with some basketball
club graduates today. Wanna come with?

01:29.112 --> 01:30.559
Oh! Of course I'll come!

01:31.209 --> 01:33.431
This is not a good time to get involved.

01:34.061 --> 01:35.253
No can do, then.

01:38.925 --> 01:40.065
Karaoke, huh?

01:40.947 --> 01:42.747
Talk about having no boundaries.

01:44.669 --> 01:45.975
Yamada's coming too.

01:46.060 --> 01:47.060
Really?!

01:47.613 --> 01:49.729
Hm? The basketball club!

01:50.670 --> 01:52.056
The boys' team is here too?!

01:52.696 --> 01:54.608
Alright, we're going on ahead!

02:00.902 --> 02:01.902
I shouldn't.

02:05.572 --> 02:06.791
I really shouldn't!

02:08.497 --> 02:09.257
This...

02:13.230 --> 02:14.230
This is...

02:15.466 --> 02:17.819
This is a major creepy move.

02:19.948 --> 02:21.902
What in the world am I doing?

02:28.348 --> 02:30.105
Alright, Yamada, you're up next.

02:32.025 --> 02:33.318
You're still eating?

02:33.679 --> 02:35.170
Then, once again,

02:35.596 --> 02:37.209
everyone grab your glasses!

02:37.933 --> 02:40.403
Here's to Kobayashi's three-pointers!

02:40.690 --> 02:42.560
Cheers!

02:43.793 --> 02:45.208
Now then, Yamada...

02:46.481 --> 02:47.721
How are you always eating?!

02:51.387 --> 02:53.448
That... was awfully close.

02:53.873 --> 02:54.873
I'm in deep waters.

02:54.873 --> 02:56.458
Who asked for melon soda again?

02:58.499 --> 02:59.358
Isn't that...

02:59.863 --> 03:01.435
Oh, aren't you the speech guy?

03:02.922 --> 03:03.922
It is him!

03:04.041 --> 03:05.840
We couldn't stop talking about it!

03:05.937 --> 03:07.383
Was it made up on the spot?

03:07.730 --> 03:09.611
Right, come on, sing with us!

03:10.051 --> 03:11.238
Get in there!

03:15.695 --> 03:16.695
I-Ichikawa?

03:18.895 --> 03:19.895
Why are you here?

03:20.155 --> 03:21.076
Huh?

03:26.949 --> 03:27.949
I'm dead.

03:28.979 --> 03:32.893
I'm officially a creepy stalker
spying on a fun party.

03:34.144 --> 03:35.144
I am...

03:48.435 --> 03:50.542
What're you doing?
You were having fun, right?

03:51.235 --> 03:52.235
I was, but...

03:53.142 --> 03:54.241
I, uh, you see...

03:54.734 --> 03:56.566
I quit halfway through, you see?

03:57.059 --> 03:59.105
I'm kind of an outsider anyway...

03:59.672 --> 04:02.150
That aside, Ichikawa, what're you doing?

04:04.323 --> 04:06.176
Should I pretend it's a coincidence?

04:06.632 --> 04:09.151
Nah, anyone can figure out
I wouldn't go to karaoke alone.

04:13.661 --> 04:14.661
Did you maybe...

04:17.156 --> 04:18.156
follow me here?

04:20.649 --> 04:21.827
N-No, umm...

04:22.186 --> 04:25.672
I was w-worried...
I mean, not really, but...

04:31.861 --> 04:32.861
Ichikawa...

04:34.762 --> 04:37.343
"I already have someone I like"...

04:37.725 --> 04:39.264
Did you hear me say that?

04:43.617 --> 04:44.617
T-That is...

04:46.047 --> 04:46.833
Now?

04:47.500 --> 04:48.500
That is...

04:49.940 --> 04:51.480
Once I put it into words...

04:52.015 --> 04:54.145
It's kinda making my heart skip a beat

04:54.836 --> 04:57.882
and making me realize my feelings more.

04:58.375 --> 04:59.728
It makes me go "woah"...

04:59.846 --> 05:02.356
And I've been acting
all funny since morning...

05:05.294 --> 05:06.294
Sorry!

05:06.914 --> 05:08.200
I don't quite get it...

05:08.629 --> 05:11.429
But that's what's happening,
so you don't have to worry.

05:12.815 --> 05:13.815
I'm...

05:14.348 --> 05:16.685
No, that's not what I was worried about...

05:18.806 --> 05:19.806
I need to face it.

05:20.441 --> 05:22.167
My own creepy behavior.

05:23.686 --> 05:24.816
The boys' basketball team is here

05:25.199 --> 05:28.121
and I don't like that, so I was worried.

05:33.789 --> 05:34.789
Sorry.

05:54.160 --> 05:55.160
How...

05:55.819 --> 05:57.562
...did I end up here?

05:58.635 --> 06:03.618
The world that you showed me

06:04.030 --> 06:09.335
was extraordinarily beautiful....

07:31.397 --> 07:33.530
Yesterday was terrible.

07:34.010 --> 07:36.805
As expected of the basketball team,
those bright, positive folks.

07:37.165 --> 07:38.165
I was shown no mercy.

07:42.628 --> 07:46.433
Well, here's to Ichikawa's
marvelous farewell speech...

07:46.950 --> 07:48.769
Cheers!

07:49.658 --> 07:52.061
Well, they weren't that bad...

07:53.369 --> 07:54.369
Ichikawa!

07:55.035 --> 07:56.035
Great timing.

07:56.393 --> 07:57.811
Huh? Hara?

07:58.690 --> 07:59.690
You know...

08:00.090 --> 08:02.180
...I kinda have something to tell you.

08:03.334 --> 08:04.407
W-What's going on?

08:07.703 --> 08:08.602
She's also here?

08:08.602 --> 08:10.550
Oh, you too, Yamada.

08:11.282 --> 08:14.286
What?! Sweets Paradise?!
Of course I wanna go!

08:14.804 --> 08:16.151
I'm glad.

08:16.553 --> 08:17.553
And then, um.

08:18.020 --> 08:20.523
Is it okay if Kanzaki comes too?

08:21.012 --> 08:22.449
Huh? That means...

08:25.003 --> 08:26.003
We're in sync.

08:27.087 --> 08:28.087
Umm, but...

08:28.648 --> 08:29.648
In that case,

08:29.968 --> 08:31.595
won't we be interrupting?

08:31.599 --> 08:33.698
Your... your date?

08:34.207 --> 08:36.500
No, I'm not sure why,

08:36.827 --> 08:39.865
but Kanzaki asked me to
bring you along, Yamada.

08:41.381 --> 08:42.381
I wonder why.

08:42.592 --> 08:43.419
And anyway,

08:43.659 --> 08:46.366
the two of you are always
hanging out together somewhere.

08:46.774 --> 08:48.660
Since when has this girl...

08:49.769 --> 08:50.769
Umm,

08:50.984 --> 08:52.570
I'm just trying to confirm, but

08:52.874 --> 08:54.640
are you guys dating?

08:55.035 --> 08:56.714
No, no, not at all.

08:56.901 --> 08:58.928
You guys are always hanging out,

08:59.242 --> 09:00.645
but you're still not dating?

09:03.324 --> 09:04.157
What is it?

09:04.310 --> 09:06.833
If you don't mind, Hara, I'm in.

09:07.155 --> 09:09.522
And you can always ditch
Yamada if she gets in the way.

09:10.922 --> 09:13.400
No, wait. Ichikawa, won't you join us?

09:14.642 --> 09:16.062
After all, Saturday is...

09:16.828 --> 09:18.488
...the 14th of March.

09:21.736 --> 09:23.062
White day!

09:24.171 --> 09:25.524
I'll go if I can.

09:25.651 --> 09:26.651
Oh, he'll go!

09:27.027 --> 09:28.027
He will?

09:28.558 --> 09:29.577
Also, like...

09:30.495 --> 09:31.831
They said they'll come along.

09:32.065 --> 09:34.321
Oh, that's great.

09:35.514 --> 09:36.514
Ichikawa, you too.

09:38.650 --> 09:40.183
So this is...

09:41.421 --> 09:42.521
...a double date?

09:45.870 --> 09:46.969
I'm looking forward to it.

09:52.290 --> 09:54.010
And so the big day is here.

09:54.616 --> 09:56.238
I'll be arriving early again...

09:56.805 --> 09:57.845
Ichikawa.

10:02.476 --> 10:03.476
Casual clothes.

10:04.029 --> 10:05.613
Guess we're taking the same train.

10:06.347 --> 10:09.505
It's still a bit early,
so I thought I'd be the only one here.

10:09.804 --> 10:10.568
Umm..

10:11.298 --> 10:13.036
I thought I'll go shopping or something.

10:13.690 --> 10:14.913
For White Day?

10:15.406 --> 10:18.531
Huh? No, it's not like...

10:19.300 --> 10:22.493
But to be honest,
I still don't know what to do.

10:23.054 --> 10:24.161
I guess you wouldn't.

10:24.902 --> 10:26.582
It's Yamada, after all.

10:26.804 --> 10:27.804
Exactly.

10:29.326 --> 10:30.580
I knew it.

10:30.796 --> 10:32.042
Why did I spill the secret?

10:32.666 --> 10:34.652
I guess it's fine if it's Hara.

10:35.638 --> 10:38.124
The more I think about it,
the more unsure I get.

10:38.830 --> 10:40.075
When I search online,

10:40.557 --> 10:42.720
all I see is stuff about
gifts that won't work.

10:43.340 --> 10:44.340
I get it.

10:45.413 --> 10:48.117
I may not be of much help,

10:48.379 --> 10:49.945
but we can look for something together.

10:50.920 --> 10:51.920
No, but...

10:52.347 --> 10:53.426
Harajuku.

10:53.426 --> 10:54.820
Oh, we're here!

10:55.322 --> 10:57.780
(Harajuku)

11:03.089 --> 11:05.608
Is this situation okay?

11:06.168 --> 11:08.388
You can't go wrong with something to eat.

11:09.179 --> 11:12.228
Nah, Yamada's always
eating good stuff, so...

11:12.778 --> 11:13.818
I guess you're right.

11:14.022 --> 11:16.604
And something handmade would look creepy

11:16.979 --> 11:18.579
or like, seem too much, right?

11:18.990 --> 11:21.266
Hm... you think so?

11:21.887 --> 11:24.180
What did Yamada give you?

11:25.368 --> 11:27.814
Something like a chocolate muffin.

11:28.180 --> 11:29.180
Was it handmade?

11:29.180 --> 11:29.940
Yeah.

11:30.419 --> 11:31.419
How did it make you feel?

11:31.694 --> 11:33.074
Huh? I mean...

11:33.374 --> 11:34.634
I-It made me happy.

11:35.234 --> 11:38.325
But there's a difference between
Yamada's handmade and mine.

11:38.974 --> 11:40.240
You think so?

11:43.673 --> 11:46.274
Accessories...
That's as creepy as it gets.

11:49.419 --> 11:50.761
We all have our preferences, after all.

11:54.261 --> 11:56.601
Should I just give her
something from a catalogue?

11:57.096 --> 11:59.460
That's for new year's gifts...

12:02.435 --> 12:04.234
All I'm being is negative.

12:04.541 --> 12:05.448
Sorry.

12:07.128 --> 12:09.310
I feel like that too, so I get it.

12:11.189 --> 12:13.220
We're kind of similar.

12:13.760 --> 12:14.823
Huh?

12:14.823 --> 12:16.429
What does that mean? Scary.

12:17.153 --> 12:17.987
Oh!

12:25.527 --> 12:26.647
How about a hat?

12:27.290 --> 12:29.263
Yamada in a hat... hmm...

12:29.866 --> 12:30.878
- Ichikawa!
- Looks cute!

12:31.399 --> 12:32.399
I think...

12:33.628 --> 12:34.379
Huh?

12:35.071 --> 12:36.005
Huh?

12:40.326 --> 12:41.469
Huuh?

12:43.447 --> 12:45.011
Wow!

12:45.011 --> 12:46.157
He's right!

12:46.741 --> 12:48.552
Hara, you look so cute!

12:49.678 --> 12:50.406
Doesn't she?

12:50.975 --> 12:51.679
Is this...

12:52.408 --> 12:53.408
Is this...

12:54.150 --> 12:55.867
Jealousy?

12:56.511 --> 12:59.532
Murder, murder, murder, murder,  murder...

12:59.532 --> 13:01.337
No, no, no, no.

13:01.740 --> 13:04.963
W-Why is this guy here
before the meeting time too?

13:05.205 --> 13:07.871
Yamada, you look super cute too!

13:08.114 --> 13:09.114
Right?

13:09.508 --> 13:11.459
She's cute, right? Isn't she?

13:12.875 --> 13:13.875
Hara...

13:14.371 --> 13:16.280
Oh, we're all here!

13:17.110 --> 13:18.616
Let's go then!

13:18.683 --> 13:22.106
Murder, murder, murder, murder, murder...

13:22.106 --> 13:23.179
My feelings...

13:23.968 --> 13:26.209
are getting all mixed up.

13:30.201 --> 13:31.269
I'll have this too.

13:31.541 --> 13:33.021
Which one to choose?

13:35.526 --> 13:37.139
Hara's so cute.

13:37.587 --> 13:39.651
- Yeah.
- Don't you agree with me!

13:39.651 --> 13:41.115
- Huh?
- At times like this, say...

13:41.230 --> 13:42.261
"She seems nice."

13:42.354 --> 13:44.034
Now, give it a try.

13:45.700 --> 13:47.661
Hara sure seems nice...

13:47.958 --> 13:49.592
Quit looking at her like that.

13:51.038 --> 13:51.638
Good.

13:51.925 --> 13:53.511
I wanna go home.

13:54.313 --> 13:58.022
That "cute" wasn't directed
at Hara in the first place...

13:58.748 --> 14:00.161
Sorry to keep you waiting.

14:02.790 --> 14:03.790
Hara,

14:03.843 --> 14:05.599
this is my treat, so please eat more.

14:05.887 --> 14:06.633
Oh, it is?

14:06.644 --> 14:09.166
No, no, I'm good.  My stomach's full.

14:13.225 --> 14:14.798
A sound from the depths of the earth.

14:15.725 --> 14:16.817
She's always like this,

14:17.356 --> 14:18.876
that's why I invited Yamada too.

14:19.385 --> 14:23.304
I thought that if Yamada's here,
Hara would eat more too.

14:25.734 --> 14:28.584
Hara, you're plenty cute just as you are!

14:30.630 --> 14:32.490
You called her cute! Amazing!

14:33.042 --> 14:34.755
I mean, she is.

14:35.204 --> 14:37.983
Kanzaki says it all the time...

14:38.117 --> 14:40.763
Huh! That's amazing!

14:41.486 --> 14:42.420
Must be nice.

14:45.566 --> 14:47.226
Here, have some fries. Eat up!

14:48.055 --> 14:49.175
No thanks...

14:49.182 --> 14:50.182
Why though?

14:50.463 --> 14:52.766
- I told you already, you're cute as...
-Stop it.

14:53.703 --> 14:56.217
When you tell someone they're
fine the way they are,

14:56.767 --> 14:59.393
unless they also think the same,
it's just us forcing what we want.

15:00.316 --> 15:01.836
If they feel that they want to change,

15:02.016 --> 15:03.016
we shouldn't invalidate that.

15:05.277 --> 15:06.277
That's right.

15:06.580 --> 15:08.894
I'm also here because I want to change.

15:10.087 --> 15:11.127
I guess you're right.

15:11.926 --> 15:12.926
But...

15:13.200 --> 15:15.321
Hara, whether you gain or lose weight,

15:15.321 --> 15:16.554
my feelings will not change.

15:18.106 --> 15:19.701
Hara, you always look happy
once you've eaten your fill.

15:19.701 --> 15:20.701
That's why I like you.

15:24.413 --> 15:25.413
Here.

15:25.799 --> 15:26.581
For you.

15:26.773 --> 15:27.773
W-What's he doing?

15:31.514 --> 15:33.225
Oh, how cute!

15:33.433 --> 15:34.792
A cutlery set!

15:37.074 --> 15:39.351
You've gone and said all that,

15:39.351 --> 15:40.861
so I guess I have to eat now.

15:42.717 --> 15:43.980
Sho good!

15:46.654 --> 15:48.490
Huh? Yamada chose it?

15:49.069 --> 15:51.580
Yeah. I knew she'd have good taste.

15:52.285 --> 15:55.079
Truth is, I came early today and
didn't know what to buy.

15:55.595 --> 15:59.346
But then I happened to run into Yamada,
and she helped me choose.

16:00.389 --> 16:02.575
Yamada is surprisingly easy to talk to.

16:02.730 --> 16:03.730
Don't talk to her.

16:03.730 --> 16:05.069
She also eats a lot, which is nice.

16:05.071 --> 16:06.071
Don't look at her.

16:07.225 --> 16:08.878
Don't go shopping with her.

16:09.756 --> 16:12.156
This guy has something I don't.

16:13.764 --> 16:15.225
Oh, I see!

16:15.317 --> 16:16.657
She's a celebrity, after all, right?

16:16.657 --> 16:18.567
No. That's not it.

16:19.753 --> 16:20.426
Ya...

16:21.230 --> 16:22.547
Yamada's mine.

16:29.427 --> 16:30.900
No, I mean...

16:31.574 --> 16:32.574
Yamada's mine...

16:32.879 --> 16:33.879
...m-min...

16:34.212 --> 16:37.258
...mind-bogglingly into
that curry I also like!

16:44.318 --> 16:46.130
It's not that Kanzaki is superior.

16:46.587 --> 16:47.900
It's that I'm inferior.

16:48.333 --> 16:49.333
As a man.

16:50.146 --> 16:51.358
So that's how it was.

16:51.812 --> 16:53.238
You feel that way about Yamada.

16:53.538 --> 16:54.538
Laughable, right?

16:55.178 --> 16:56.578
Someone like me with Yamada...

16:57.745 --> 16:59.005
She's too out of my league.

16:59.352 --> 17:00.482
You think so?

17:01.089 --> 17:03.149
Everyone says
you're a great guy, Ichikawa,

17:03.645 --> 17:05.061
and your speech was awesome, too.

17:06.022 --> 17:07.755
You've got your own identity about you.

17:08.036 --> 17:09.036
It's cool.

17:09.415 --> 17:10.415
Now that I think about it,

17:10.820 --> 17:12.282
you and her might be a great match.

17:14.277 --> 17:16.116
W-What about you, h-huh?

17:16.329 --> 17:18.157
C-C-Confess already.

17:18.728 --> 17:20.474
I already have!

17:21.957 --> 17:23.323
You mean that earlier?

17:24.202 --> 17:26.854
But for some reason my feelings
don't really come across right...

17:27.608 --> 17:30.694
If this goes on, I'll keep on wondering
whether we're actually dating or not.

17:31.061 --> 17:33.489
Like those relationships adults have.

17:34.890 --> 17:36.343
Well, that's fine too!

17:36.981 --> 17:41.051
It seems this guy might be missing
that crucial something too.

17:41.333 --> 17:42.573
Huh?

17:45.135 --> 17:47.488
Seem like Yamada is lost!

17:48.094 --> 17:50.387
What's with this see-throughable act?

17:52.139 --> 17:54.191
L-Let's split up and look for her.

17:54.528 --> 17:56.394
We're gonna go look over there.

17:56.394 --> 17:58.082
Ichikawa, please help over there.

17:58.082 --> 17:59.970
Huh? Uh, but...

17:59.970 --> 18:01.290
Just do it!

18:11.626 --> 18:12.826
Not very smooth, are you?

18:13.367 --> 18:14.367
What do you mean?

18:14.650 --> 18:15.650
Nothing...

18:21.995 --> 18:22.995
In the end,

18:23.397 --> 18:25.670
even if we're both out together,

18:26.132 --> 18:28.698
we just want to be all by ourselves.

18:31.171 --> 18:33.362
No, no, I mean, this is about those two!

18:33.362 --> 18:34.405
Uh, um...

18:37.182 --> 18:39.382
What are you doing after this?

18:44.664 --> 18:45.664
Going home, I guess.

18:48.072 --> 18:49.072
I see.

18:50.420 --> 18:51.420
Yeah, let's do that.

18:52.189 --> 18:53.189
I'm done for the day.

19:00.368 --> 19:02.830
I'm always comparing myself to others.

19:03.538 --> 19:06.161
I get jealous and self-deprecate
over trivial things.

19:07.263 --> 19:08.657
I don't want to keep being like this.

19:12.279 --> 19:13.279
Stop it.

19:13.496 --> 19:14.616
Have you forgotten already?

19:15.302 --> 19:18.089
Who is it that believes in you the most?

19:35.566 --> 19:36.683
Is there a valuable item

19:37.406 --> 19:38.406
in there?

19:41.205 --> 19:43.194
("We Are...")

19:46.685 --> 19:47.685
Yamada...

19:49.333 --> 19:50.333
What is it?

19:51.232 --> 19:52.734
O-Once we're at the station...

19:53.724 --> 19:54.724
Just for a bit...

19:55.076 --> 19:57.025
("...Overflowing")

19:59.353 --> 20:02.258
Those two are in
a pair seat at a net cafe!

20:02.910 --> 20:05.163
How grown-up of them.

20:07.325 --> 20:08.238
But...

20:09.019 --> 20:11.497
I like this vibe.

20:14.763 --> 20:15.763
I see...

20:16.478 --> 20:18.230
During Valentine's day, Yamada...

20:19.780 --> 20:21.673
...was giving so much effort.

20:23.889 --> 20:25.562
Comparisons, jealousy,

20:26.101 --> 20:27.652
they're just defense mechanisms.

20:28.408 --> 20:29.408
You idiot.

20:29.670 --> 20:30.816
Don't look at anything else.

20:32.197 --> 20:33.400
Kyotaro Ichikawa,

20:34.396 --> 20:35.396
don't you dare...

20:36.176 --> 20:39.289
...think of anything... but Yamada.

20:40.432 --> 20:41.432
Here.

20:50.363 --> 20:52.289
A muffin! You'll share it with me?!

20:54.644 --> 20:55.644
You must be disappointed.

20:55.996 --> 20:57.663
No, no, not at all.

20:57.737 --> 20:58.737
Did you make it?

20:59.099 --> 21:01.099
I was there when it was being made.

21:01.809 --> 21:03.302
I guess they call that foreshadowing.

21:04.281 --> 21:06.180
Even though I'm sure you must be full...

21:11.794 --> 21:12.907
Take it easy!

21:13.098 --> 21:14.138
Shorry, shorry.

21:14.458 --> 21:16.138
I'm just sho happy.

21:33.687 --> 21:36.447
Accessories are as creepy as it gets.

21:37.552 --> 21:39.985
Like Hara said,
everyone has their preferences...

21:57.776 --> 21:58.390
Hey.

22:04.573 --> 22:05.573
Put it on for me.

22:21.860 --> 22:22.860
How does it look?

22:24.540 --> 22:25.547
So...

22:28.158 --> 22:29.423
So cute I could die.

22:33.060 --> 22:34.060
I love you.

22:35.220 --> 22:36.220
I do.

22:36.711 --> 22:37.711
I do.

22:43.127 --> 22:44.127
Huh?

22:44.814 --> 22:46.494
Why am I...

22:47.974 --> 22:49.695
These tears are not the same as back then.

22:50.914 --> 22:51.914
We've taken just a few

22:52.553 --> 22:53.730
very important steps forward.

22:55.207 --> 22:56.207
This is...

22:56.595 --> 22:57.734
...our vibe.

23:00.590 --> 23:03.179
("We Are Overflowing")
